Joachim von zur Gathen and Jürgen Gerhard, Modern Computer Algebra, third edition, Cambridge University Press, 2013. Bibliographic and theorem-location details unverified, also cited in (`credit:nrz:cas-polynomial-literature`). Supports rational-function arithmetic, gcd/Bezout certificates, square-free decomposition, polynomial factorization distinctions and algebraic extensions. Concrete arithmetic-wrapper and memory-budget behavior must be established by later implementation evidence rather than by citing this text.

**Attribution (Dynamic evaluation)** · `credit:nrz:cas-solving-dynamic-literature`

J. Della Dora, C. Dicrescenzo and D. Duval, “About a New Method for Computing in Algebraic Number Fields,” EUROCAL '85, volume II, Lecture Notes in Computer Science 204, first proceedings edition, Springer, 1985. This recalled record, including author spellings, title and volume details, is unverified. It motivates dynamic evaluation through splits discovered during algebraic computation. The graph split and its gcd/product/Bezout proof obligations are argued here independently; no algorithm layout or code is taken from a system using that technique.

